{"id":493,"date":"2020-10-27T13:32:46","date_gmt":"2020-10-27T20:32:46","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=493"},"modified":"2024-08-30T10:06:02","modified_gmt":"2024-08-30T17:06:02","slug":"493","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/493\/","title":{"rendered":"1B: Flight Directions"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213df934c2\" name=\"6a2213df934c2\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Getting Started<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Make sure that your CoDrone Mini is paired before starting the lesson! If you forgot how to do this, make sure to review how to pair to Blockly <a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/cdmb-pairing\/\">here<\/a>.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213df935f4\" name=\"6a2213df935f4\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Flight directions<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Air vehicles move a little differently than land vehicles. While land vehicles can move forward, backward, and sometimes side-to-side, air vehicles can do all of that and move up and down! There are two blocks in the flight commands menu in Blockly that can help you program your CoDrone Mini to fly in any of these directions.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;494&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213df93650\" name=\"6a2213df93650\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Go for a certain amount of time<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">One of the blocks you can use will make your drone move in the direction you pick for a certain amount of time. All you need to do is drag the go _ for _ seconds block from the flight commands menu to your workspace, pick your direction from the drop-down menu, and then type in the seconds you want your CoDrone Mini to travel for. The default power for this block is set to 50%, which means that it will fly at 50% of the CoDrone Mini&#8217;s full speed.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;498&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213df9369d\" name=\"6a2213df9369d\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Go for a certain amount of time...now with power!<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you know how fast (or slow!) you want your CoDrone Mini to go, you can use a different block! Select the go _ for _ seconds at _ % power block from the flight commands menu, and then use the drop-down menu to pick your CoDrone Mini\u2019s direction. Type in your CoDrone Mini\u2019s flight time as well as the power value. This number can range from 0 to 100, with 0 being completely still and 100 being very fast. We recommend starting at 50 and seeing what you need to do from there.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;501&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213df936f0\" name=\"6a2213df936f0\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Turn for a certain amount of time<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In addition to being able to fly up, down, left, right, forward, and backward, your CoDrone Mini can also turn left and right! The turn _ for _ seconds at _ % power block allows you to control how much time your drone spends turning. Drag it to your workspace, and then pick left or right from the drop-down menu. Type in the number of seconds you would like your CoDrone Mini to turn for, and then type in the power value. This number can range from 0 to 100, with 0 being completely still and 100 being very fast. We recommend starting at 50 and seeing what you need to do from there.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;502&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213df93737\" name=\"6a2213df93737\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Put it all together!<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Try writing a program that will have your CoDrone Mini take off, fly forward, and then turn before landing! It could look something like the example code in the image.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;503&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213df93782\" name=\"6a2213df93782\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<b>Challenge: Shapeshifter<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Have your CoDrone fly in a shape (triangle, quadrilateral, pentagon, hexagon, octagon, etc.) using all of the commands you just learned! The only rule is that you HAVE to include a kill switch.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 8 Getting Started [vc_column_text]Make sure that your CoDrone Mini is paired before starting the lesson! If you forgot how to do this, make sure to review how to&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/493\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1687,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":true,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":407,"_lesson_preview":""},"lesson-category":[1817,1763,1777,1793,626,1533,1438,853,144,167,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2108,2125,2115,2123,2124,2122],"class_list":["post-493","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-blockly","lesson-tag-codrone-mini","lesson-tag-flight-directions","lesson-tag-fundamentals","lesson-tag-junior","lesson-tag-programming","module-junior","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/493","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":9,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/493\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":12813,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/493\/revisions\/12813"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1687"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=493"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=493"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=493"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}